  "notes": "**Hutsix v3.6.0**(released)\n\n### Triggers\n- **Fixed: screen-based triggers never used the shared screenshot, so each one captured the whole desktop itself.** A monitor has two names \u2014 the one the calibrator stores (`dxgi-0-0`) and the Windows device name (`\\\\.\\DISPLAY1`) \u2014 and the capture service only recognised the second, so every screen, pixel, OCR and AI trigger asked for a monitor it could not find and fell back to its own full-screen capture. A trigger set to check ten times a second was really checking about twice, and the extra captures cost a visible slice of a CPU core.\n- Those triggers now read one shared capture per tick, sized to the areas the bindings watch instead of the whole desktop: reading an area from it costs about 0.01 ms instead of 1.7 ms, and a fast binding runs at roughly 33 checks per second instead of 5.\n- The debug log now records when the shared capture has no frame for a monitor, so a fallback like this cannot stay invisible.",
